,{"id":"e164","layer":"L1","type":"frame","x":1424,"y":1662,"w":852,"h":608,"text":"Behind the query verbs","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e147","layer":"L1","type":"frame","x":14,"y":1302,"w":1302,"h":684,"text":"3 Front end","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e69","layer":"L1","type":"frame","x":14,"y":822,"w":3402,"h":369,"text":"2 Compile pipeline (C4.exe)","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e38","layer":"L1","type":"frame","x":14,"y":22,"w":1632,"h":614,"text":"1 Toolchain","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e1","layer":"L1","type":"text","x":0,"y":-470,"w":682.7,"h":52,"text":"C4 compiler: architecture review","fontSize":40,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e2","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":0,"y":-390,"w":1000,"h":190,"text":"What this board shows: how C4.exe turns a whole program into one executable, the tools built on the same library, and the review of 2026-11-20 with what came of it.\nRead in order: 1 Toolchain -> 2 Pipeline -> 3-7 each phase, inside (5b Program lowering, 5c MIR are new) -> 8 Tools -> 9 Runtime contract -> 10 Review (table R1-R16 on the layer 'Review table', and the order of work).\nGreen notes: what was done, with commits. Every box has a desc (hover it, or read the plan).\nStatus 2026-11-25: all sixteen review points done, verified, pushed and deployed. Open: BUG-509, this machine's hardware.","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e3","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1060,"y":-390,"w":520,"h":190,"text":"Legend\nblue: compiler code (C4Lib)  |  indigo: executables and tools on it\norange hexagon: external (LLVM, clang, lld, OS)\ngreen cylinder: caches and files on disk\nviolet parallelogram: data handed between phases\nteal: runtime and default library\nnotes: red = high, orange = medium, yellow = low priority, green = keep as is","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e4","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":60,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"Nuke","color":"indigo","desc":"Python build system at the repo root: reads nuke.toml, writes projects.toml and the LSP options per program, runs C4.exe once per program, runs nuke gates.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e5","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":360,"y":60,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"IED + c4 plugin","color":"indigo","desc":"The IDE. Talks LSP to C4LSP and DAP to C4DAP; builds through Nuke.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e6","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":680,"y":60,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"Script host program","color":"gray","desc":"A user's C4 program built with --script-host; loads C4Script.dll and compiles .cf scripts at run time against its .c4i interface.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e7","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1000,"y":60,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"External tools","color":"gray","desc":"Linters, doc generators, asset pipelines: use the C API of C4Api.dll.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e8","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":220,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"C4.exe driver","color":"indigo","desc":"C4/src/Source.cpp CompilerDriver::Run: register sources, preprocess, parse, model, RunBackend -> ProgramBackend::Lower (ProgramLowering::Run, then ProgramEmitter::Emit), ProgramOutput (optimize, objects, link).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e9","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":360,"y":220,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"C4LSP","color":"indigo","desc":"C4LSPLib: CompilationSession runs phases 1-5 (no LLVM) per program; features answer from the ProgramModel.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e10","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":680,"y":220,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"C4Script.dll","color":"indigo","desc":"Embedded compiler for scripts: ScriptCompiler (script-mode lowering), ScriptJit (LLVM ORCv2), ScriptHost (load, guarded calls, reload).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e11","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1000,"y":220,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"C4Api.dll","color":"indigo","desc":"C interface for tools, API v1: parse one source, declarations and syntax diagnostics only.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e12","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1400,"y":220,"w":220,"h":60,"text":"C4DAP","color":"indigo","desc":"C4DAPLib: a debugger over the Win32 debug API and DbgHelp, reading the CodeView/.pdb the compiler writes. Does not link C4Lib.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e13","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":380,"w":1180,"h":70,"text":"C4Lib: the compiler as a C++ library","color":"blue","fill":"blue","fontSize":20,"desc":"Static library, namespace C4Compiler (R14): SourceManager, Macro, Interop, Lexer, Parser, Compiler (CompilerInstance), Model, Backend/Lowering, Backend/HIR, Backend/MIR, Backend/CodeGen, Backend/Reflection, Target, Script, Outline. Links Core, Reflection, ObjectDescription, Profiling and LLVM.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e14","layer":"L1","type":"hexagon","x":1400,"y":380,"w":220,"h":70,"text":"Win32 debug API + DbgHelp","color":"orange","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e15","layer":"L1","type":"hexagon","x":40,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"LLVM 22","color":"orange","desc":"Vendored, linked statically: IR, PassBuilder -O pipeline, X86 backend, bitcode, ORCv2 JIT.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e16","layer":"L1","type":"hexagon","x":290,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"clang","color":"orange","desc":"Bundled: compiles extern \"c\"/\"c++\" source files, C++ shims and the runtime's C sources.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e17","layer":"L1","type":"hexagon","x":540,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"lld-link","color":"orange","desc":"Links partitions, runtime objects, foreign objects and libraries; /DEBUG writes the .pdb.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e18","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":790,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"CBind.exe","color":"indigo","desc":"clang libtooling subprocess: a C/C++ header in, C4 declarations (+ C++ shims) out; cached as .c4bind.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e19","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1040,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"C4Runtime","color":"teal","desc":"C/C++ runtime linked into every program: GC, reflection registry, RTTI walk, EH, threads/TLS, static storage, test runner, script runtime, platform (Win32 + Posix).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e20","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1290,"y":540,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"Bedrock","color":"teal","desc":"The default library, C4 source: compiled with every program from the install's Bedrock/bedrock.ch umbrella; prelude.ch declares the runtime's entry points.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e21","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e5","to":"e4","text":"build, test","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e22","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e4","to":"e8","text":"runs per program","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e23","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e5","to":"e9","text":"LSP","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e24","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e5","to":"e12","text":"DAP","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e25","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e6","to":"e10","text":"compile scripts","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e26","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e7","to":"e11","text":"C API","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e27","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e8","to":"e13","text":"links","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e28","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e9","to":"e13","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e29","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e10","to":"e13","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e30","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e11","to":"e13","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e31","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e12","to":"e14","text":"reads .pdb","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e32","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e15","text":"IR, -O, objects","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e33","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e16","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e34","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e17","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e35","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e18","text":"bindings","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e36","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e19","text":"builds, links","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e37","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e13","to":"e20","text":"compiles","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e39","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"1 Register sources","color":"blue","desc":"SourceManager (C4/src RegisterSources): CLI folders scanned recursively for .cf/.ch, --projects (projects.toml), the Bedrock umbrella and only what bedrock.ch reaches, the prelude. Only .cf files are entry files. Reads on several threads.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e40","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":390,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"2 MacroPass","color":"blue","desc":"Macro/ (R8): expansion over tokens, a MacroLayout per file (each file expanded once; a header expands the same for every includer; tables flow down includes). The file's text is never rewritten.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e41","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":740,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"3 InteropPass","color":"blue","desc":"Interop/ (R8): extern \"c\"/\"c++\" include|source. CBind per header -> a binding unit the includer includes; clang per foreign source; libs. Any failure is a hard error.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e42","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1090,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"4 Parse (parallel)","color":"blue","desc":"CompilerInstance::CompileAll: every file lexed (through its MacroLayout) and parsed exactly once on all threads; the parser recovers per declaration (R7). include parks the requester until the header is parsed; closures folded. LSP reuses unchanged parses (PriorParses).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e43","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1440,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"5 Program model","color":"blue","desc":"ModelBuilder: pass 1 registers shells, pass 2 resolves to a fixed point (<= 64 rounds), body references instantiate templates (<= 8 rounds), FinalizeLayouts, CheckObjectTypes, AnnotationCheck. One ProgramModel; one thread.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e44","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1790,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"6 HIR lowering","color":"blue","desc":"Backend/Lowering ProgramLowering (R2) decides what lowers: written bodies, reachable template-made and compiler-written functions (D-16), thunks, global starts; LowerFunction (Backend/HIR) per body, batches on ParallelLowering's threads. Same pass in C4.exe, C4LSP and scripts. Output: LoweredProgram.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e45","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2140,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"7 LLVM emission","color":"blue","desc":"ProgramEmitter (R3, emit-only): every unit of the LoweredProgram into its partition, shared vtables, harness or @main, starts, globals, reflection, census counters, imports, nounwind, finish, verify. --incremental: emitted straight into partitions.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e46","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2490,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"8 Optimize + assemble","color":"blue","desc":"R12: one emission path. Debug/Development: each partition optimized alone with copies of small callees; Dist: partitions merged (PartitionMerge), optimized whole, split for parallel code generation. X86 backend on -j threads; objects named by bitcode hash and reused.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e47","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2840,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":"9 Runtime + link","color":"blue","desc":"RuntimeObjects: every C4Runtime .c/.cpp compiled by clang at -O2, cached by content. LinkWithLLD: partitions + runtime + foreign objects + libs, libcmt, /DEBUG for -g.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e48","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":3190,"y":860,"w":200,"h":70,"text":".exe + .pdb","color":"violet","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e49","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e39","to":"e40","text":"source texts","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e50","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e40","to":"e41","text":"MacroLayout","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e51","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e41","to":"e42","text":"binding units","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e52","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e42","to":"e43","text":"AST + closures","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e53","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e43","to":"e44","text":"ProgramModel","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e54","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e44","to":"e45","text":"HIR trees","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e55","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e45","to":"e46","text":"llvm::Module(s)","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e56","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e46","to":"e47","text":".obj each","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e57","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e47","to":"e48","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e58","layer":"L1","type":"cylinder","x":740,"y":1030,"w":200,"h":80,"text":"Interop cache","color":"green","desc":"<int>/<out>.interop/: .c4bind per header and flags, foreign objects keyed by source + depfile headers + flags + clang (ForeignCache).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e59","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2140,"y":1030,"w":200,"h":70,"text":".ll / .bc","color":"violet","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e60","layer":"L1","type":"cylinder","x":2490,"y":1030,"w":200,"h":80,"text":"Object cache","color":"green","desc":"<int>/<out>.objects/<hash>.obj: key = partition bitcode + compiler identity + target settings; claims per pid so two compilers can share it (BUG-442/443).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e61","layer":"L1","type":"cylinder","x":2840,"y":1030,"w":200,"h":80,"text":"Runtime objects","color":"green","desc":"%TEMP%/c4_runtime/<hash of runtime folder>/O2, each object named for its source and header bytes.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e62","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":3190,"y":1030,"w":200,"h":70,"text":".c4i + inline bodies","color":"violet","desc":"--script-host: the host's interface (files without non-template bodies, macros, symbols, reflected types) and the bitcode of functions scripts may inline.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e63","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e41","to":"e58","style":"dashed","start":"arrow","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e64","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e45","to":"e59","text":"-S, -bc","style":"dashed","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e65","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e46","to":"e60","style":"dashed","start":"arrow","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e66","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e47","to":"e61","style":"dashed","start":"arrow","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e67","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e46","to":"e62","text":"--script-host","style":"dashed","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e68","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":40,"y":1030,"w":640,"h":130,"text":"Threads: register N, parse N, model 1, HIR -j in rounds, emission per partition, optimize/assemble -j, link 1.\nStop points: any parse or model error stops before 6; any lowering error stops before 7 (first 16 shown).\nIED server, 16 threads: one-statement edit 1.85 s at -O0, 3.25 s at -O3 (roadmap 5.3).","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e123","layer":"L1","type":"text","x":0,"y":1210,"w":276.3,"h":36.4,"text":"Each phase, inside","fontSize":28,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e124","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":1350,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"SourceManager","color":"blue","desc":"Source = one file's text, never rewritten (R8), + its line table. SourceInfo: absPath, project, macros (its MacroLayout), binding (a binding unit) and bindings (the binding units it includes). Registration of files/folders/projects, ResolveInclude (beside the file, its project, its dependencies, the library), RegisterBinding.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e125","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":1350,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Preprocessor","color":"blue","desc":"R8: expansion over tokens. Compiler/SourceMacros -> MacroPass (each file once; tables flow down includes through SourceManager::ResolveInclude, so a header expands the same for every includer) -> Preprocessor (lines, uses, directives) -> MacroToken (file offset, spaceBefore) -> MacroExpander/MacroSubstitution (paste, stringize, placemarkers). Out per file: FileResult {MacroLayout (regions left out + each MacroExpansion: macro, where defined, its pieces and where the file spells them), table, exported, diagnostics}. MacroLayout::Render gives text where text is needed (interface files, interop, tools).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e126","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":1350,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"InteropPass","color":"blue","desc":"R8: InteropSources finds the files whose text or expansions hold extern; InteropPass runs CBind per header (C4 declarations + C++ shims) and clang per source; each bound header becomes a binding unit (SourceManager::RegisterBinding, registered once) that its includer includes - no text is appended to any file.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e127","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":1510,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"CompilationUnit","color":"blue","desc":"One per file: its AST root, include list, transitive include closure; IncludeBindings includes its binding units as headers (R8); StartReplay when a prior parse is reused (same text + layout + bindings).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e128","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":1510,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"CompilerInstance","color":"blue","desc":"Owns one compilation: sources, units, the parallel parse scheduler (queue, parked units, deadlock release, include cycles), phase times, the ProgramModel and its error trackers.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e129","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":1510,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Message queue","color":"blue","desc":"CompilerMessageQueue: RequestFileInclude messages from parsing units; the requester parks until the header is parsed, then its closure is folded in.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e130","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":1670,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Lexer","color":"blue","desc":"Lexer(Source, id, MacroLayout*) reads the file through its layout (R8): every token's location is its spelling location (file line, column, byte offset) plus its expansion site (SourceLocation::expansion, clang's model); SourceLocation::Before orders tokens of one use; Token::FollowsDirectly forms compound operators; template-aware >> splitting; LexerRecovery for speculative parses; BraceRecovery (R7) pairs braces by indentation.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e131","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":1670,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Parser","color":"blue","desc":"Parser/: one node type per file, TryParse + ParseBody; PrattParser for expressions. R7: Parser/Recovery SkipBroken per declaration (file, namespace), member and statement; ErrorNode in the tree; one diagnostic per mistake; every declaration that parsed stays in the unit, so the model registers it and includers see no cascade.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e132","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":1670,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"ErrorTracker","color":"blue","desc":"Diagnostics with suppression frames, so a rolled-back speculative parse never leaks an error; ReportOncePerLocation. DiagnosticReporter renders file (line:col) error: message with context, the same list for CLI and LSP.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e133","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":1830,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"PriorParses (LSP)","color":"blue","desc":"The language server's next analysis takes the trees of files whose text (written and expanded) did not change; C4.exe never does.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e134","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":370,"y":1830,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"AST per file","color":"violet","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e135","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e124","to":"e125","text":"texts","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e136","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e125","to":"e126","text":"layouts","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e137","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e128","to":"e127","text":"per file","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e138","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e127","to":"e130","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e139","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e130","to":"e131","text":"tokens","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e140","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e131","to":"e134","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e141","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e131","to":"e132","text":"errors","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e142","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e129","to":"e128","text":"includes","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e143","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e133","to":"e134","text":"reused","style":"dashed","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e144","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":1340,"w":330,"h":245,"text":"Done R8 (chat B, 75ce8e8e): files are never rewritten. Macros expand over tokens into a MacroLayout per file; every token keeps its spelling location and its expansion site, so diagnostics say 'in the expansion of X, defined at f:l' and BUG-446's column mapping (ColumnMap) is gone. CBind output is a binding unit the includer includes. Preprocess 0.144 -> 0.099 s on the IED server.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e126","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e145","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":1600,"w":330,"h":120,"text":"Keep: parse-once with include closures is the program model's core: each header is one unit, parsed once, on all threads (front end ~0.1 s on the Bedrock tests).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e129","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e146","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":1735,"w":330,"h":225,"text":"Done R7 (chat B, cabed2f3): the parser recovers per declaration, member and statement (Parser/Recovery, ErrorNode, BraceRecovery by indentation): one error per mistake, the rest of the file parses and is registered, so includers report no cascade. (The model never skipped such units; the doc was stale.) Found: Bedrock's array.ch never closed its namespace.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e132","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e148","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1450,"y":1350,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"ModelBuilder (pass 1)","color":"blue","desc":"Model/Builder: registers every top-level declaration of every unit as a shell (types incomplete, names in the scope tree, template definitions, pending work lists). Order never matters. Then visits the prelude and records include closures.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e149","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1730,"y":1350,"w":275.2,"h":64,"text":"DeclarationQueries (pass 2)","color":"blue","desc":"R9: one sweep in declaration order over memoized per-declaration queries (Model/Builder/DeclarationQueries); resolving a declaration first resolves what it names (alias target, enum values, variable type, object parts via ObjectMemberResolver, methods a definition belongs to); in-progress marks report cycles with their path. ModelResolver says how one declaration resolves; FreeFunctionResolver for free, extension and out-of-line functions. Then body references, FinalizeLayouts, CheckObjectTypes.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e150","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2010,"y":1350,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"AnnotationCheck","color":"blue","desc":"Folds the annotations of every reflected entity after the layouts; declared annotations (annotation Range(...) on field) matched as overloads.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e151","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1700,"y":1500,"w":300,"h":80,"text":"ProgramModel","color":"blue","fill":"blue","fontSize":20,"desc":"One per compilation. Query verbs: ResolveType, QueryType, QueryFunction (free, methods, operators by name, constructors; overloads and templates inside), QueryOperator, QueryVariable, QueryMember, QueryConstant, SizeOf/AlignOf, RecordFor. Errors are QueryResult values with a message and location. LookupContext {unit, enclosingType, scope, receiver access}.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e152","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1450,"y":1700,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"TypeStore","color":"blue","desc":"Owns every Type* for the compilation; builtins, pointers, references, arrays, funcptrs, signatures interned so pointer identity is type identity; caches read under a shared lock.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e153","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1730,"y":1700,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"SymbolTable","color":"blue","desc":"Scope tree File > Namespace > Class > Function > Block; SymbolInfo per name; every FunctionRecord with its stable mangled symbol; per-unit include closures; ScopeCursor per lowering thread.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e154","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2010,"y":1700,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"SymbolQueries","color":"blue","desc":"Every name query: SymbolTable::IsVisible / FindVisible - one rule for declarations and bodies (R4, D-88): the declaring file is the asking file or in its transitive includes; templates through TemplateDef::unit; an instance's names from its template's file (LookupUnit, Scope::FindBound). Model/NotIncluded writes the error naming the header to include. Member lookup across bases, InheritedSignatureClash, SelectByReceiverAccess.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e155","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1450,"y":1860,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"TypeResolver","color":"blue","desc":"Every type position: aliases, qualified paths, specializations, const layers (ApplyIndirections), return lists.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e156","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1730,"y":1860,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"OverloadResolver","color":"blue","desc":"One ranking for functions, methods, operators, constructors: arity filter, ParamCost sum, written beats template instance, partial ordering between instances, else Ambiguous.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e157","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2010,"y":1860,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"Templates","color":"blue","desc":"TemplateInstantiator + Model/Templates: arguments, deduction, packs, specializations, partial ordering, member templates, ObjectTemplateBody. Bindings are fake aliases in a scope layer; instances cached by value; no AST substitution.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e158","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1450,"y":2020,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"ConstEvaluator","color":"blue","desc":"Folds AST constant expressions on demand: literals, arithmetic, logic, comparisons, sizeof, nameof, sizeof..., folds, references to constants; cycles report CyclicDependency. A call of a [compile_time] function (R6, D-91) goes to FoldCall -> CompileTimeEvaluator, which interprets the callee's MIR.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e159","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1730,"y":2020,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"OperatorTable","color":"blue","desc":"The one token -> canonical name catalog (- is subtract or negate by arity); OperatorAnnotations collects [operator(...)] names into FunctionRecord::operatorAnnotations.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e160","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2010,"y":2020,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"Hierarchy + vtables","color":"blue","desc":"Model/Types ClassHierarchy: LocateBase, PointerDelta, sub-object walks, base-list rules; VirtualTables: slots by name + parameter types, VptrLocations, FinalOverrider, DispatchFor. Shared by HIR and codegen. ObjectType::CalculateLayout is the one layout authority (MSVC order).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e161","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1450,"y":2180,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"Lowering scopes","color":"blue","desc":"LoweringScopes: RAII PushScope/ScopeGuard, RegisterLocal(Type/Alias/Function) for bodies being lowered; Closures: CreateClosure / ClosureMadeFor for lambdas.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e162","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1730,"y":2180,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"ModelMaking (requests)","color":"blue","desc":"R10: Model/ModelMaking replaces ModelWrites/ModelFrozen. A change while bodies lower is a request: one maker at a time, readers take no lock, double-checked find / Request / find / make; answers shown when the outermost request ends; a write outside a request while lowerings share the model is an internal compiler error. Grow-only tables: Model/Concurrent (GrowOnlyMap, GrowOnlyList, MadeTables).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e163","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2010,"y":2180,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"Types (15 kinds)","color":"blue","desc":"Primitive, Pointer, Reference, Array, FunPtr, Function, Object, Union, Enum, Alias, Swizzle, InitList, TemplateParam, TemplateSpecialization, Invalid. TypeHandle wraps a Type* with capability queries.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e165","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e148","to":"e151","text":"shells","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e166","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e149","to":"e151","text":"resolves","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e167","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e150","to":"e151","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e168","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e151","to":"e164","text":"friends","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e169","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2310,"y":1340,"w":340,"h":265,"text":"Done R9 (chat C, 65633bc1): pass 2 is one sweep in declaration order over memoized queries (Model/Builder/DeclarationQueries): a declaration first resolves what it names; a cycle is reported with its path (A -> B -> A). The 64 + 8 round caps are gone; template recursion stops at c_MaxInstantiationDepth with an error. Model phase 0.210 -> 0.167 s (IED server). Fixed BUG-478/479/480; found BUG-481.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e149","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e170","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2310,"y":1620,"w":340,"h":120,"text":"Keep: one model, a handful of query verbs, errors as values, one operator catalog, one overload ranking. This design ended the old drift bugs.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e151","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e171","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2310,"y":1755,"w":340,"h":250,"text":"Done R4 (chat C, 67db64d8, D-88): one rule in SymbolTable::IsVisible - a name is visible where its file is the asking file or in its includes, for declarations as for bodies. A template instance resolves in its template's file (so it does not depend on who asks first). Error: 'no type named Widget is visible here: it is declared in widgets.ch, which this file does not include'. Fixed BUG-476/486; includes added in Bedrock, the IED server, Claymore and AmmoCrate.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e154","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e172","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2310,"y":2020,"w":340,"h":265,"text":"Done R6 (chat G, 814e52b8, D-91): a function marked [compile_time] runs in constants - its MIR interpreted (MirInterpreter: byte memory in the target's layout, bounds-checked, 1,000,000 steps, 256 calls deep). CompileTimeCheck refuses what cannot run at compile time. Const initializers, array extents, enum values, annotation arguments, case labels and (parenthesized) template value arguments take it; what folded before folds the same.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e158","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e174","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e124","to":"e128","text":"texts, layouts, binding units","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e175","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2800,"y":1500,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"ParallelLowering","color":"blue","desc":"Backend/Lowering/ParallelLowering (R10): one pass, each body lowered once on -j threads; model changes go through ModelMaking::Request (memoized by their keys: definition + arguments, owner + lambda node, type + op, element types); ProgramModel::SharedLowering settles before and orders what was made after (OrderMade), so records and names do not depend on -j.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e176","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":2070,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"LowerFunction","color":"blue","desc":"LoweringDriver: one FunctionRecord + the model -> HIRFunction (owns its arena) + diagnostics in its own ErrorTracker. Pushes the function scope, binds parameters, pushes template bindings as fake aliases; every layer pops by RAII.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e177","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":2070,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"ModelQueries","color":"blue","desc":"The one model-facing surface of HIR: query wrappers bound to the asking context, constructor/destructor/cast lookup, token -> primitive-op maps, scope API pass-through.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e178","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":2230,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"DeclLowerer","color":"blue","desc":"Slots, reference locals, direct construction, braced starts (fields, designators, ranges), static locals (Once + AtExit), StartGlobal, BracedValue.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e179","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":2230,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"StmtLowerer","color":"blue","desc":"Statement dispatch, blocks through RegionScope (scope layer + jump path), return/if/switch/break/continue/goto/labels, statement temporaries and full expressions; one error per failed statement.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e180","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":2230,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"ExprLowerer","color":"blue","desc":"ResolveExpr(node) -> QueryResult<Value>; split by concern: access, calls, call targets, construction, operators, casts, assignment. Implicit conversions become ConvertNodes, operator calls CallNodes with the chosen record.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e181","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":2390,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Lifecycle","color":"blue","desc":"LifecycleFacts, Lifecycle (Construct, DestroyNow, ScheduleDestroy, CopyInto, CopyOf, Take, Assign, Temporary), MethodBody parts, Construction plans; fresh values relocate, views copy; PartsGuard/FillGuard for exception safety.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e182","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":2390,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Exceptions + loops","color":"blue","desc":"ExceptionLowerer (try/catch, throw, defer, finally as defer), LoopLowerer (while, for, range-for over arrays, pointers, init lists and the iterator protocol), DestructuringLowerer, FoldLowerer, PackElements, AsmLowerer.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e183","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":2390,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"LambdaLowerer","color":"blue","desc":"Plans captures (FindOuterUses, defaults, init captures, this / *this), asks the model for the closure type, lowers the body at once as the closure's call method (nested HIRFunction).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e184","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":2550,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"GlobalInit","color":"blue","desc":"One round of __c4_global_init: globals and static members not yet started, in unit and source order, each in its own unit and scope; ConstantImage turns a constant-only start into initial data.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e185","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":2550,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Post-body checks","color":"blue","desc":"After a body lowers: JumpScopes::Validate (goto rules) and access checks. Last-use moves, drop flags, missing return and unreachable code moved to MIR (R5, frame 5c).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e186","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":2550,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"LoweringContext","color":"blue","desc":"Per-function state: record, unit, enclosing type, slots, BindLocal / LocalValue, break and continue label stacks, defer depth, jump scopes, coercions, Fail/Report. LoadIfNeeded is the one lvalue-to-rvalue place.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e187","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":370,"y":2710,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"HIRFunction tree","color":"violet","desc":"Closed node taxonomy (~45 node kinds), every node concretely typed; LValue descriptors (Slot, Field, Base, Global, This, Deref, Lane, Swizzle, IndexOp); complete == false is never emitted.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e189","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e176","to":"e179","text":"body","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e190","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e179","to":"e178","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e191","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e179","to":"e180","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e192","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e179","to":"e182","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e193","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e180","to":"e183","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e194","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e178","to":"e181","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e195","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e182","to":"e185","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e196","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e185","to":"e187","text":"complete tree","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e197","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e177","to":"e173","text":"query verbs","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e198","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":2200,"w":340,"h":275,"text":"Done R10 (chat I, cf2faf93): lowering's model changes are requests (Model/ModelMaking: one maker at a time, readers lock-free, answers shown when a request ends; grow-only tables in Model/Concurrent). Every body lowers once, in one pass, on threads - no rounds, no cap, no serial fallback; output identical at -j 1 and 16. Thread-sanitizer gate on Linux (tsan_unit.py) found and fixed BUG-492/493/494. Claymore lower 1.42 -> 1.31 s.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e175","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e199","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":2490,"w":340,"h":270,"text":"Done R5 (a3230ae2): MIR (frame 5c) is built from each HIR tree where lowering runs, so the editor sees its diagnostics too. Moves, drop flags, missing return and unreachable code are passes on the CFG, and codegen emits from MIR with one EH lowering per TargetAbi scheme. R6 next: CTFE interprets MIR.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e185","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e200","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":960,"y":2775,"w":340,"h":120,"text":"Keep: HIR is the one place bodies are checked, by the build and the editor alike; nodes carry concrete types so codegen never re-derives semantics.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e176","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e202","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1430,"y":2450,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ProgramEmitter","color":"blue","fill":"blue","desc":"Emit-only (R3). Called by ProgramBackend after ProgramLowering::Run: prepare partitions, file asm, declare written functions, emit every lowered unit into its partition (partitions at once), shared vtables, harness or @main, starts, materialize globals, reflection, census counters, check that codegen named nothing lowering did not lower, imports, nounwind, finish, verify.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e203","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1760,"y":2450,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ModuleContext","color":"blue","desc":"The module; the one C4 -> LLVM type map; struct creation from the model's offsets; function signatures; global storage; runtime entry points; MakeLocal for split programs.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e204","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2090,"y":2450,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"Abi + TargetAbi","color":"blue","desc":"Abi: the calling-convention brick; it no longer knows the system - it asks the TargetAbi (AggregateRegisters, VectorPassesInMemory, MemberReturnsObjectsInMemory, SretBeforeThis, MemoryArgumentsOnStack). TargetAbi (C4Lib/src/Target/, R11): one immutable instance per system, picked once per build (CpuTarget::Abi, ModuleContext::Target): WindowsX64Target (MSVC-shaped) and LinuxX64Target (D-86); AggregateRegisters (Win64, System V eightbytes).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e205","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1430,"y":2610,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"FunctionEmitter","color":"blue","desc":"Entry block, slot allocas, parameter binding, runs the MirEmitter over the function's MIR, nested functions as siblings; EmitImport for available_externally copies.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e206","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1760,"y":2610,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"MirEmitter","color":"blue","desc":"R5: emits a function from its MIR: blocks and edges as they are, cleanups and unwinds from the MIR's explicit edges; the EH scheme through EhLowering (FuncletLowering on Windows, LandingPadLowering on Linux), chosen by the TargetAbi. Replaces RegionEmitter, RegionLandingPads and CleanupStack.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e207","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2090,"y":2610,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"Expr + Call emitters","color":"blue","desc":"ExprEmitter (rvalues, lvalue addresses incl. lanes and base sub-objects, conversions, GcStore), ExprOperatorEmitter, CallEmitter (hidden params, Abi per argument, direct/virtual/indirect), SimdEmitter, AtomicEmitter, AsmEmitter.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e208","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1430,"y":2770,"w":246.9,"h":64,"text":"IRContext + EH lowering","color":"blue","desc":"IRBuilder, entry-block allocas, this, sret, the ONE call brick (funclet bundle + invoke); EhLowering: FuncletLowering (catchswitch, cleanuppad) or LandingPadLowering, one per TargetAbi scheme (R5).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e209","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1760,"y":2770,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"Object model emitters","color":"blue","desc":"ObjectEmitter (new, temporaries, init lists, delete), VtableEmitter (one table per vptr, this-adjusting thunks, c4_purecall), RttiEmitter (MSVC TypeDescriptor, hierarchy, locators), EhTables (ThrowInfo), MsvcNames, PeTables.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e210","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2090,"y":2770,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"DebugInfo + TBAA","color":"blue","desc":"-g: DIBuilder CodeView (Windows) or DWARF 5 (Linux): subprograms, locals at slots, types, globals, a line per statement. AliasClass/AliasTags: !tbaa strict aliasing (D-64).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e211","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1430,"y":2930,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"PartitionSet + imports","color":"blue","desc":"PartitionSet: the partition modules, placement (ProgramPlacement), emission on threads, each partition's census counters. ImportEmitter: available_externally copies of small callees (ImportPlanner's rule). StableNames keep names independent of order.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e212","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1760,"y":2930,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ReflectionEmitter","color":"blue","desc":"Invoke and type thunks -> partition locals, invoke/type entries, the image (RegistrationEmitter describes what ReflectionScope keeps, ReflectionTables builds), the D-82 key and its own module; __c4_reflect_init.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e213","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2090,"y":2930,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"StartupEmitter","color":"blue","desc":"__c4_global_init and thread-start rounds, StartAsData, script init and first-use starts, @main or the -test harness, GC stats; GcRoots, census types (from lowering's counters), InferNoUnwind, TargetAttributes, VectorAlignment.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e214","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e202","to":"e203","text":"owns","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e215","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e203","to":"e204","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e216","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e202","to":"e205","text":"per tree","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e217","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e205","to":"e206","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e218","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e206","to":"e207","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e219","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e205","to":"e208","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e220","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e206","to":"e209","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e221","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e207","to":"e210","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e222","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2370,"y":2440,"w":340,"h":240,"text":"Done R3 (24892b9b): CodeGenDriver (~80 methods, 37 fields) is gone. Lowering decides what is emitted (frame 5b); codegen only emits: ProgramEmitter (the assembly order), PartitionSet, StartupEmitter, ReflectionEmitter, ImportEmitter, with ProgramBackend as the facade C4.exe and scripts call. LoweredProgram is the seam where a MIR (R5) goes.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e202","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e223","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2370,"y":2700,"w":340,"h":230,"text":"Done R11 (chat D, d9e31bf1): one TargetAbi per build in C4Lib/src/Target (WindowsX64Target, LinuxX64Target). Abi, IRContext::Funclets, ModuleContext, DebugInfo, ObjectEmission, BuildUtils, RuntimeObjects and the link ask it instead of branching on the system. Output byte-identical (32 of 32 files, Windows and Linux, -O0/-O2, +-g); Linux suites pass. Found BUG-484: a Windows install had no ld.lld.exe, so no Linux program linked.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e209","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e224","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2370,"y":2950,"w":340,"h":170,"text":"Done R13 (chat H, 84b10f8c, D-89): reflection is opt-out, never silently: [reflect(\"off\")] on a declaration or namespace block, or reflect = \"off\" per project; the default stays everything. Out of scope = no registration, thunks or unneeded storage. Serializing an out-of-scope type is a compile error. IED server opted out as a test: image 15.9 -> 12.0 MB, exe 24.6 -> 21.8 MB.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e212","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e226","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2840,"y":2450,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"ProgramOutput","color":"blue","desc":"C4/src/ProgramOutput (R12): WritePartitions (Debug, Development: each partition optimized alone, small callees copied), WriteWholeProgram (Dist: Merged - partitions merged, optimized whole, split for code generation), WriteModule (-S, -bc, -c, scripts: one partition); objects through the cache; the reflection image's keyed module; script-host interface and inline bodies; runtime objects; the TargetAbi's link.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e227","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3150,"y":2450,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"Toolchain","color":"blue","desc":"Compiler/Toolchain: clang, lld, the runtime sources, CBind and Bedrock from the install C4.exe runs from; WindowsSysroot from setup.bat's kit.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e228","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2840,"y":2610,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"OptimizeModule","color":"blue","desc":"PassBuilder default pipeline at -O<n> (O0 pipeline at -O0) with the build's TargetMachine; C4 runs no optimization pass of its own. Debug/Development: each partition alone on its thread; Dist: the merged module whole.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e229","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3150,"y":2610,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"ModulePartitions","color":"blue","desc":"Dist only (R12): the optimized whole module split again for parallel code generation (by source file with -g, by name otherwise; data no file names alone in partition 0).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e230","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2840,"y":2770,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"WriteCachedObjects","color":"blue","desc":"X86 backend per partition on up to -j threads; a partition whose object the cache keeps is not assembled; identical partitions share one object.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e231","layer":"L1","type":"cylinder","x":3150,"y":2765,"w":240,"h":80,"text":"ObjectCache","color":"green","desc":"Key: hash of the partition's bitcode + the compiler's identity read from its running image (BUG-508: no longer from the file by path) + target settings. A link that fails while cached objects are in it assembles them again and links once more; an object that came out different is kept in <int>/<name>.rejected/. Claims per pid let two compilers share the folder; only the latest build's objects are kept.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e232","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2840,"y":2930,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"RuntimeObjects","color":"blue","desc":"Every C4Runtime .c/.cpp compiled with clang -O2 -Werror on demand, keyed by its bytes and every runtime header's.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e233","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3150,"y":2930,"w":240,"h":64,"text":"LinkWithLLD","color":"blue","desc":"The link is the TargetAbi's (R11): Windows lld-link in process (objects, runtime, interop objects, libs, -l/-L/-Wl, libcmt, oldnames, clang runtime libs, /SUBSYSTEM:CONSOLE, /DEBUG /PDB for -g); Linux ld.lld against the Debian 11 sysroot (shipped in every install since BUG-484).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e234","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e226","to":"e227","text":"finds tools","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e235","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e226","to":"e228","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e236","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e228","to":"e229","text":"split","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e237","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e228","to":"e230","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e238","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e230","to":"e231","text":"reuse","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e239","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e230","to":"e232","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e240","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e232","to":"e233","text":"objects","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e241","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":3450,"y":2700,"w":330,"h":280,"text":"Done R12 (chat H, 5af1a6f3, D-90): one emission path. Every linked build emits into partitions. Debug/Development optimize each alone and copy small callees (PartitionCopies). Dist merges its partitions (PartitionMerge, at most 16, so -j never changes it), optimizes the one module whole, then splits it for code generation. PartitionImports and the whole-module split's copy modes are gone. Run-time speed equal; builds same or faster (Development edit 7.0 -> 5.6 s).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e229","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e243","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1000,"y":1030,"w":1080,"h":135,"text":"Done R1 (chats O, S, W): stage 1 up to 256 partitions (53eeff3c); stage 2a a build server, Nuke's default for Debug and Development (bde92795): body edits re-lower their bodies, re-emit their partitions and relink; stage 2b (f6b4f6af): globals' values, inline and template bodies served too. Byte-identical to a one-shot build (Serve.* 29/29). IED server -O3: string edit 2.2 -> 1.0 s, header constant 2.9 -> 1.8 s; Claymore editor 5.0 -> 2.4 s. Signatures, types, includes, macros stay cold (docs/compiler/07). Idle server holds its last build (~6-9 GB, 30 min).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e42","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e244","layer":"L1","type":"text","x":0,"y":3200,"w":299.6,"h":36.4,"text":"Around the compiler","fontSize":28,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e245","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":3340,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"LspServer","color":"indigo","desc":"C4LSPLib Server/: stdio transport, MessageInbox, ProgramPlan (as few programs as hold the open documents, B75), analyzes only the programs that changed, merges cross-program results, answers completion from the last analysis while one runs.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e246","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":3340,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"CompilationSession","color":"indigo","desc":"Per program: registers sources like C4.exe, macro pass, interop declarations only, CompileAll with PriorParses, AnalyzeProgram, then RunLoweringPass = ProgramLowering::Run (the build's own lowering, no emission) for body diagnostics.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e247","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":40,"y":3500,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"LSP features","color":"indigo","desc":"Features/: definition, declaration, references, rename, hover, completion (members, includes, annotations), semantic tokens, symbols, call and type hierarchy, code actions, missing definitions, c4/expandMacro.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e248","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":370,"y":3500,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"SemanticResolver","color":"indigo","desc":"NodeLocator finds the AST path at a position; SemanticResolver drives the model's own query verbs with the scope context of that path. A missing fact becomes a new model query, never LSP logic.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e249","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":3340,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ScriptHost","color":"indigo","desc":"C4Script.dll: load, guarded calls (a crashing script does not take the host down), unload, reload; Bedrock's Scripting::Host / Script wrap it.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e250","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":700,"y":3500,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ScriptCompiler","color":"indigo","desc":"ScriptSources registers the host's interface files and the script's; ProgramBackend in script mode (ScriptLowering: host bodies lowered only when reached), inline bodies imported available_externally, ScriptModulePasses, the PassBuilder pipeline.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e251","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1030,"y":3500,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"ScriptJit (ORCv2)","color":"indigo","desc":"One LLJIT per script with the host's __c4_script_table as its symbol source; memory manager, unwind tables, EH glue, emulated thread storage.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e252","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":1030,"y":3340,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"Host .c4i","color":"violet","desc":"The host's interface: projects, files with interface text and exported macros, symbols, reflected types; plus the inline bodies' bitcode.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e253","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1360,"y":3340,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"C4Api v1-v3","color":"indigo","desc":"v1: c4a_parse_source - one source's declarations and syntax diagnostics. v2 (R15): c4a_program_open (sources or a projects description, defines, the install) analyzes a whole program through C4LSPLib's CompilationSession; then diagnostics, resolve (a name at a position), type_at, references, members_of / members_at; plain C structs, strings owned by the handle, errors as values. Sample: plugins/c4/samples/c4-query.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e254","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1360,"y":3500,"w":230,"h":64,"text":"C4DAP engine","color":"indigo","desc":"Own debugger over the Win32 debug API and DbgHelp: one engine thread, int3 patches, line steps from registers, values by CodeView types with C4 names, stops in the catch a throw lands in (MSVC EH tables). Launch only.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e255","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e245","to":"e246","text":"per program","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e256","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e245","to":"e247","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e257","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e247","to":"e248","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e258","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e248","to":"e246","text":"model","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e259","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e249","to":"e250","text":"compile","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e260","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e250","to":"e251","text":"module","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e261","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e252","to":"e250","text":"interface","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e262","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1680,"y":3330,"w":360,"h":290,"text":"Done R2 (24892b9b, BUG-482): the copied loop's script filter skipped every template-made record, so the editor never lowered ANY template-made body and missed 5 of 7 body errors a build reports. CompilationSession::RunLoweringPass now runs ProgramLowering::Run (no emission), with the build's script-host setting from Nuke's LSP options. Test Lsp.LoweringParity 9/9.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e246","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e263","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1680,"y":3640,"w":360,"h":140,"text":"Done R15 (chat P, 330e8a06, 0aad2eee; chat R, 4199b58d): C4Api v2 - a whole program's model through the C API: diagnostics, what a name resolves to, the type at a position, references, a type's members. v3 adds members with their bases' (c4a_program_members_with_bases_of) and a declarations-only open (C4A_OPEN_DECLARATIONS_ONLY). It reuses the language server's analysis and resolver, so a tool sees what the editor and the build see.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e253","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e265","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":3340,"w":280,"h":64,"text":"__c4_gc_roots","color":"violet","desc":"{address, size, pointers} of every global, static member and static local whose type may hold a managed pointer (pointers = its map, null = read whole; R16 phase 2), ended by {null, 0}; __c4_gc_thread_roots likewise for each thread_local.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e266","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":3480,"w":314.1,"h":64,"text":"Typed + precise allocations","color":"violet","desc":"new -> c4_alloc_precise(size, align, census record) for a type with a pointer map (PointerMaps: one bit per 8-byte word that may hold a managed pointer); new T[n] -> c4_alloc_precise_array (record + size class); c4_alloc_typed for a type whose every word may; _noscan for pointer-free types. gc_type_of(T) names a type's record for typed buffers (c4_gc_register_typed_region, c4_buffer_resize_scanned_typed); c4_type_info carries it for reflected values.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e267","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":3620,"w":280,"h":64,"text":"Reflection image","color":"violet","desc":"__c4_reflect_init (priority 65534) registers the image under -reflect-tag: types, fields, methods, enums, globals, functions, annotations, invoke and type thunks.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e268","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":3760,"w":280,"h":64,"text":"RTTI + EH tables","color":"violet","desc":"MSVC TypeDescriptors, hierarchy descriptors, CompleteObjectLocators, ThrowInfo; on Linux landing pads on libgcc's unwinder with field-relative references.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e269","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":3900,"w":280,"h":64,"text":"Starts and exits","color":"violet","desc":"__c4_global_init rounds in @llvm.global_ctors, __c4_thread_start, Once regions, AtExit registrations, @main wrapper or the -test harness.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e270","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":2190,"y":4040,"w":280,"h":64,"text":"Script table","color":"violet","desc":"--script-host: __c4_script_table (every symbol a script may bind), thread-local accessors, shared vtables named by type.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e271","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2640,"y":3410,"w":260,"h":64,"text":"GC","color":"teal","desc":"C4Runtime/GC: non-moving mark-sweep over every attached thread; per-thread allocation caches; parallel marking; concurrent marking past 16 MiB live; pools; census; default trigger 115%. Precise: heap objects by their type's map, typed regions, roots, and - by default since 26e5f261 - every C4 frame by its stack map (records by return address); runtime, C and script frames and Windows funclet calls read whole.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e272","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2640,"y":3620,"w":260,"h":64,"text":"Reflection registry","color":"teal","desc":"C4Runtime/Reflect: thread-safe handle-based registry, stacked registrations for scripts, unload listeners.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e273","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2640,"y":3760,"w":260,"h":64,"text":"RTTI + EH runtime","color":"teal","desc":"RttiRuntimeC (c4_instance_of, c4_dynamic_cast), EHRuntime.cpp, ExceptionsPosix.c, uncaught-exception reporting.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e274","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2640,"y":3900,"w":260,"h":64,"text":"Static storage + threads","color":"teal","desc":"StaticStorageRuntimeC + shim (once guards, exit-time destruction), ThreadRuntime (Win32/Posix), thread storage starts and ends, test runner.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e275","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2640,"y":4040,"w":260,"h":64,"text":"Script runtime","color":"teal","desc":"ScriptRuntimeC + Script/: per-script exit lists, emulated TLS, script images and their throws, GC root tables and finalizer dropping per code range.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e276","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e265","to":"e271","text":"roots","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e277","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e266","to":"e271","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e278","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e267","to":"e272","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e279","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e268","to":"e273","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e280","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e269","to":"e274","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e281","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e270","to":"e275","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e282","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2980,"y":3330,"w":360,"h":275,"text":"Done R16 (chats F, K, X). Precise heap objects, roots, typed buffers and reflected values. Stack maps on by default on Windows and Linux (26e5f261, f17a7a63): each call's live values named in place, C4's own compact format (the IED server's map 107 MB -> 2 MB). Run time at parity; exe +4-10%; compile time: 16 threads -O0 0..+1%, -O2 0%; one thread -O0 +5-9%. -fno-stack-maps byte-identical to before. Fixed BUG-504..507. Owner: the host keeps a Script reachable.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e271","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e283","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2980,"y":3620,"w":360,"h":150,"text":"The runtime contract: what the compiler emits on the left is read by the C runtime on the right. Every C4 program links all of C4Runtime (cached objects, -O2).","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e285","layer":"L1","type":"text","x":0,"y":4300,"w":401.3,"h":36.4,"text":"10 Review: what to change","fontSize":28,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e286","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":40,"y":4380,"w":830,"h":170,"text":"The yardstick - what C4 needs from its compiler:\n1 a whole-program model with include visibility (parse-once headers)  2 fast edit-compile-run on a 1000-file engine\n3 the editor reports exactly what the build reports  4 reflection, scripts and hot reload on one type system\n5 compile-time evaluation and richer templates  6 GC plus value lifecycle (relocation, last-use moves)\n7 Windows today, Linux next (D-86), more targets later","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e287","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":900,"y":4380,"w":830,"h":170,"text":"Keep as is: the whole-program model with parse-once includes; one ProgramModel behind query verbs; HIR as the only place bodies are checked; stable, order-independent names (object cache, scripts); in-process LLVM with partitioned, cached objects; the ten architecture principles of docs/compiler/README; the gates (C4Testing 1121, e2e, negative, isolated, differential against clang). Only 4 bugs are open (known-bugs, next BUG-478).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e288","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":4660,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"1  R2: one lowering driver","color":"green","fill":"green","desc":"Extract ProgramLowering (work list, ParallelLowering, global-init rounds, thunk planning) from CodeGenDriver; C4.exe, C4LSP and ScriptCompiler call it. Add a test that the LSP and C4.exe report the same errors for an unused template member.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e289","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":4660,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"2  R3: split CodeGenDriver","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e290","layer":"L1","type":"diamond","x":1880,"y":4790,"w":379.2,"h":100,"text":"3  R4: decided - one rule","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e291","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":4960,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"4  R7 + R8: robust front end","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e292","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":5090,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"5  R9 + R10 done","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e293","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":5090,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"6  R1 done","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e294","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":5220,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"R15: C4Api queries","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e295","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":5350,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"7  R5: MIR (CFG)","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e296","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":5480,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"8  R6: CTFE on MIR","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e297","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":5480,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"R16 done (stacks: flag)","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e298","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":1880,"y":5610,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"9  R11: TargetAbi with B31","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e299","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":5610,"w":320,"h":64,"text":"R12, R13, R14 done","color":"green","fill":"green","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e300","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e288","to":"e289","text":"then","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e301","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e292","to":"e293","text":"enables","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e302","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e293","to":"e294","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e303","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e295","to":"e296","text":"interprets","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e304","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e295","to":"e297","text":"escape analysis","style":"dashed","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e305","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1880,"y":5740,"w":740,"h":110,"text":"Order: 1-2 are small and remove drift now. 3 is a language decision. 4-6 make the edit loop and the editor scale. 7-8 open CTFE and better moves. 9 rides the Linux port. Arrows are real dependencies.","color":"gray","fill":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e307","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4640,"w":70,"h":50,"text":"#","color":"gray","fill":"gray","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e308","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4640,"w":120,"h":50,"text":"Priority","color":"gray","fill":"gray","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e309","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4640,"w":430,"h":50,"text":"Change","color":"gray","fill":"gray","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e310","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4640,"w":760,"h":50,"text":"Why it matters for C4","color":"gray","fill":"gray","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e311","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4640,"w":300,"h":50,"text":"Where","color":"gray","fill":"gray","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e312","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4690,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R1","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e313","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4690,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e314","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4690,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Incremental front end: cached parses, declaration fingerprints, HIR per function","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e315","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4690,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Edit-compile-run on a 1000-file engine is bound by re-parsing, re-modelling and re-lowering everything; Bedrock is rebuilt every build.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e316","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4690,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"CompilerInstance, ModelBuilder, LSP (B76)","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e317","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4766,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R2","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e318","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4766,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e319","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4766,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"One ProgramLowering shared by C4.exe, C4LSP and scripts","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e320","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4766,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"The editor must report what the build reports; the LSP's hand copy of the lowering loop already differs (template members).","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e321","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4766,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"CodeGenDriver, CompilationSession, ScriptCompiler","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e322","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4842,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R3","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e323","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4842,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e324","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4842,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Split CodeGenDriver; codegen becomes emit-only","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e325","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4842,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"~80 methods and 37 fields in one class: scripts, partitions, reflection and startup all land there, so each change costs more and risks more.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e326","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4842,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"Backend/CodeGen/CodeGenDriver","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e327","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4918,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R4","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e328","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4918,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e329","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4918,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"One visibility rule: declarations see only what their file includes","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e330","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4918,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Headers can lean on files they never include, and a template is callable where a plain function is not (BUG-476, BUG-440).","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e331","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4918,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"SymbolQueries, ModelBuilder","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e332","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":4994,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R5","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e333","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":4994,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e334","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":4994,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"A control-flow-graph IR (MIR) between HIR and LLVM","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e335","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":4994,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Moves, drop flags, definite init, missing return and cleanups are separate tree walks; a CFG gives them one home and enables escape analysis.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e336","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":4994,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"HIR post-body passes, RegionEmitter","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e337","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":5070,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R6","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e338","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":5070,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e339","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":5070,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Compile-time evaluation by interpreting typed IR","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e340","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":5070,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Growing ConstEvaluator over the AST into constexpr functions would write C4's semantics a second time.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e341","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5070,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"Model/ConstEvaluator (roadmap 6)","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e342","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":5146,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R7","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e343","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":5146,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e344","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":5146,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Error-tolerant parse: keep the rest of a broken file","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e345","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":5146,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"One typo in a header drops all its declarations and cascades 'unresolved' through every includer, worst in the editor.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e346","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5146,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"Parser, ModelBuilder::Build","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e347","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":5222,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R8","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e348","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":5222,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e349","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":5222,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Token-level macros with expansion locations; bindings as their own unit","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e350","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":5222,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Rewriting file text turns positions into a mapping problem (BUG-446) and hides what came from a macro or CBind.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e351","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5222,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"Macro/, Interop/, SourceManager","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e352","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":5298,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R9","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e353","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":5298,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e354","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":5298,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Resolve declarations on demand, not in capped rounds","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e355","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":5298,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Caps of 64 and 8 rounds are magic numbers and cost rounds x declarations; demand-driven resolution is the base of R1.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e356","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5298,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"ModelBuilder, ModelResolver","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e357","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":40,"y":5374,"w":70,"h":76,"text":"R10","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e358","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":110,"y":5374,"w":120,"h":76,"text":"Done","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e359","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":230,"y":5374,"w":430,"h":76,"text":"Model changes during lowering as pure memoized requests","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e360","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":660,"y":5374,"w":760,"h":76,"text":"Freeze, retry rounds and a serial fallback limit parallel lowering and keep the model moving under the LSP and R1.","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e361","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5374,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"ModelWrites, ParallelLowering","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
