,{"id":"e391","layer":"L2","type":"rect","x":1420,"y":5830,"w":300,"h":76,"text":"GcRoots, census types, C4Runtime/GC","color":"gray","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e393","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":1720,"y":330,"w":360,"h":170,"text":"Done R14 (chat L, ec1cea28): the compiler's C++ namespace is C4Compiler (was Scripting, the name Bedrock's script API also has); docs/compiler's source tree and pages describe today's pipeline; roadmap section 5 records the review.","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"about":"e13","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e394","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":4775,"w":320,"h":56,"text":"Yes: one rule everywhere","color":"green","fill":"green","desc":"Declarations resolve through the file's include closure like bodies (SymbolQueries); headers that lean on program-wide lookup get an include. Migration: a warning first.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e395","layer":"L1","type":"round","x":2300,"y":4870,"w":320,"h":56,"text":"No: document both rules","color":"gray","style":"dashed","desc":"Keep program-wide declarations, document the two rules, and fix BUG-476 so templates follow the body rule like plain functions.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e396","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e290","to":"e394","text":"yes","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e397","layer":"L1","type":"connector","from":"e290","to":"e395","text":"no","style":"dashed","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e398","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2700,"y":4380,"w":700,"h":300,"text":"Carried out 2026-11-20..25 by chats A-AB (.ied/local/c4-work.md); WORK.md has the entries (5eb5b432, c8a8db12, d3180def).\nDONE - R1-R16, all review points: build server Nuke's default for Debug/Development, stack maps on by default, GC trigger 115%\nBugs fixed - 421, 435, 441, 476, 478-508, 510 (510: a compile no longer deletes runtime objects another build is linking, 77de5f72)\nVerified on 823e557c - C4 gates, Linux suites, IED server 571/571, conformance (559 checks), Nuke 362, frontend 508; Claymore 84/84, AmmoCrate 54/54 (Windows + Linux), JRPGToolkit, LS 81/82 (LS's own work in progress)\nPushed - IED origin/main ..d3180def; Claymore main ..c848ffd0. Deployed - ammocrate, ied-config from c8a8db12\nOpen - BUG-509: the machine's hardware (RAM/CPU: MemTest86, latest BIOS, a per-core stress test)","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e399","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2700,"y":4720,"w":700,"h":200,"text":"Done - IED tool problems found while drawing and running this work:\n- docs_read names what a docs set holds and the workspace file to fs_read (a055f93b)\n- board: a note's color tints it; a frame named in 'around' keeps its members (738f9986)\n- board tools answer after the change is on disk, so a commit right after one sees it (e21602cb)\n- search_text's missing-path hint lists a folder's files (b3a9dd83)\n- chats' messages labeled by sender; the chain-limit message says what restarts the count (4c1ad6b0, 340f9eae)","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e400","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2800,"y":1360,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"ProgramLowering","color":"blue","fill":"blue","desc":"Backend/Lowering (R2): decides WHAT lowers and in what order, no LLVM. Run: written bodies -> [--script-host: every class's vtables] -> invoke + type thunks -> loop { global starts round by round; thunks; every global's storage }. Called by C4.exe and scripts (through ProgramBackend) and by C4LSP (no emission). Result: LoweredProgram.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e401","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3130,"y":1360,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"ProgramReach","color":"blue","desc":"The D-16 closure: Need / Holds / Keep / LowerNeeded; what each lowered tree's emitted code needs is lowered next; diagnostics and use notes (an error in a template-made body names the instance and where it is first used).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e402","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3460,"y":1360,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"BodyNeeds","color":"blue","desc":"What a lowered tree's emitted code names: calls, function addresses, constructors, finalizers, exit destroyers, EH copy/destroy, held object types, census counters. Walks only the tree codegen emits (HIRWalk).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e403","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3130,"y":1500,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"Thunk plans","color":"blue","desc":"InvokeThunkPlan and TypeThunkPlan: the reflection invoke thunks and each type's construct / copy / destroy thunks, planned in lowering, emitted by ReflectionEmitter.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e404","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3460,"y":1500,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"GlobalStarts + storage","color":"blue","desc":"GlobalStarts: the __c4_global_init / thread-start rounds. GlobalStorage: every global's storage and the function a function-pointer global starts at (resolved here now, no longer in codegen).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e405","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2800,"y":1640,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"VtableEntries","color":"blue","desc":"Type -> the functions its vtables run (VtableEntry). Lowering uses it to know which virtual methods an object's vtables need (D-16); VtableEmitter::Entry calls the same function, so they cannot drift.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e406","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3130,"y":1640,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"ScriptLowering","color":"blue","desc":"The script-host predicates: a host's interface bodies are lowered only when reached, in the compile and the editor alike; Nuke's LSP options carry scriptHost so the editor lowers as the build does.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e407","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":3460,"y":1640,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"LoweredProgram","color":"violet","desc":"The seam between lowering and emission: ordered units (Function, InvokeThunk, TypeThunk, ProcessStarts, ThreadStarts, FirstUseStart), census counters, invoke uses, the type plan, function-pointer starts, the lowered set. Codegen refuses to name anything not in it (internal error).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e408","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e400","to":"e401","text":"each step","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e409","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e401","to":"e402","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e410","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e401","to":"e175","text":"batches","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e412","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2800,"y":1780,"w":950,"h":130,"text":"Done R2 + R3 (chat A, commit 24892b9b): one lowering driver. C4.exe and scripts call ProgramBackend = ProgramLowering::Run, then ProgramEmitter::Emit; C4LSP runs ProgramLowering alone. So editor errors equal build errors by construction. The old copied loop never lowered any template-made body: the editor missed 5 of 7 body errors a build reports (BUG-482; test Lsp.LoweringParity 2/7 -> 9/9). Lower phase same or faster (IED server -O0 cold 0.432 -> 0.417 s, edit 0.51 -> 0.46 s).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e414","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":40,"y":2070,"w":220,"h":64,"text":"Bodies come from 5b: ProgramLowering, on ParallelLowering's threads","color":"gray","fontSize":12,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e415","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":1430,"y":3060,"w":560,"h":64,"text":"TargetAbi (Windows | Linux)","color":"blue","fill":"blue","desc":"C4Lib/src/Target (R11). Answers every target question: triple, data layout, PIC/PIE; calling convention (Win64 / System V); EH scheme (funclets / landing pads) and personality; table anchoring; debug format (CodeView / DWARF) and the debug file; constructors in .init_array; executable and shared-library names; sysroot and foreign / runtime source flags; the link (lld-link or ld.lld) and script-host link arguments. RTTI, EH tables, MsvcNames and PeTables stay MSVC-shaped on both targets by design. ARM64 later = one more implementation.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e417","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3450,"y":2610,"w":330,"h":64,"text":"PartitionMerge (Dist)","color":"blue","desc":"Compiler/PartitionMerge (R12): reads each partition's bitcode back into one context, links them with the reflection image and a script host's table, makes the partitions' local symbols local again; the module is then optimized whole and split for parallel code generation (ModulePartitions).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e418","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e417","to":"e229","text":"Dist","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e419","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2020,"y":3060,"w":300,"h":64,"text":"ReflectionScope","color":"blue","desc":"Backend/Reflection/ReflectionScope (R13, D-89): what is reflected, read from the model only (so C4.exe, C4LSP and scripts agree). [reflect(\"off\")] / [reflect(\"on\")] on a type, function, global, static member or namespace block; a project's reflect = \"off\" (nuke.toml -> projects.toml). Nearest wins: declaration, owner type, template, namespace blocks innermost first, project. Out of scope: not registered, no thunks, no storage for a global nothing names. ReflectsCheck: Bedrock's serializers are [reflects(\"T\")] - serializing an out-of-scope type is a compile error naming the field path.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e420","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e419","to":"e212","text":"decides","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e421","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2800,"y":2045,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"MirBuilder","color":"blue","desc":"Backend/MIR (R5): builds each complete HIRFunction's MIR (HIRFunction::mir) where lowering runs - ProgramReach's Keep calls EnsureMir on ParallelLowering's threads - so its diagnostics reach C4LSP too. MirBuilderScopes turns scopes, defers and temporaries into explicit cleanup and unwind edges.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e422","layer":"L1","type":"parallelogram","x":3130,"y":2045,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"MirBody (CFG)","color":"violet","desc":"Basic blocks with explicit cleanup and unwind edges, places and moves, drops elaborated with drop flags. docs/compiler/06-mir.md.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e423","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":3460,"y":2045,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"MIR passes","color":"blue","desc":"MirReach (unreachable code, missing return, the jump rules), MirMoves (D-05 last-use moves and drop flags, the goto limitation lifted). They replace HIR's LastUseMoves and Reachability tree walks.","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e424","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e421","to":"e422","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e425","layer":"L2","type":"connector","from":"e422","to":"e423","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e426","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":3130,"y":2140,"w":620,"h":150,"text":"Done R5 (a3230ae2) and R6 (814e52b8, chat G): MIR, a control-flow graph between HIR and LLVM. Flow checks, last-use moves and drop flags run once on it; MirEmitter emits it with the TargetAbi's EH lowering. Constants run [compile_time] functions by interpreting their MIR. Speed at parity. Found BUG-485 (a DAP line table).","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e428","layer":"L1","type":"rect","x":2800,"y":2150,"w":290,"h":64,"text":"MirInterpreter (CTFE)","color":"blue","desc":"R6: CompileTimeEvaluator (one per model, set on it by CompilerInstance) lowers a [compile_time] callee once and runs its MIR in MirInterpreter over folded arguments; CompileTimeCheck (in LowerFunction) refuses new/delete, asm, statics, non-const globals, atomics, SIMD, varargs, indirect or virtual calls and unmarked callees. A global started by such a call that returns plain data starts as data (HIR/CompileTimeImage).","by":"ai"}
,{"id":"e429","layer":"L1","type":"note","x":2700,"y":4960,"w":700,"h":300,"text":"Done - open bugs and follow-ups (chat J):\n- BUG-481 fixed (28288254); BUG-487 does not reproduce (parity test d7821d68)\n- found and fixed BUG-488 (gate race), BUG-489 (scripts and [compile_time]), BUG-490 (formatter)\n- IED server tests pass in Dist; the crash was a test that went on after a failed assert (8cd8093d)\n- clangd's first search: index grace counts from the first open file (2dffb1cf)\n- 'write a call in a template argument in parentheses' (5f994f8e)\n- limits lifted: [compile_time] in pass 2, [reflects] on member templates, reflect=\"off\" reaches scripts\n- chat labels and the chain-limit message (4c1ad6b0)\nStill open: BUG-421, 435 (blocked: Claymore does not compile on F's Bedrock change), 441","color":"green","fill":"green","fontSize":14,"by":"ai"}
]
,"plans":[
{"id":"p1","title":"C4 compiler: architecture and review","kind":"markdown","text":"# C4 compiler: architecture and review\n\nStatus (2026-11-25): every review point of 2026-11-20 is done, verified, pushed (IED origin/main up to d3180def;\nClaymore main up to c848ffd0) and deployed (the NAS apps `ammocrate` and `ied-config` from c8a8db12). The work ran in\nchats A-AB, coordinated in `.ied/local/c4-work.md`; WORK.md has the entries (5eb5b432, c8a8db12, d3180def). The board's\nframes show the compiler as it is now; green notes say what changed.\n\n## 1. What the compiler is\n\n- `C4.exe` (`C4/src/Source.cpp`) compiles a **whole program in one invocation**, or, under Nuke's Debug and Development,\n  through a **build server** (`--serve-on`) that keeps the last build and rebuilds only what an edit touched. Every source\n  and the default library are parsed once, analyzed into one `ProgramModel`, lowered (ProgramLowering -> HIR -> MIR),\n  emitted into LLVM partitions, optimized, assembled into cached objects and linked by the build's TargetAbi.\n- Everything except the thin driver lives in **C4Lib** (C++ namespace `C4Compiler`), shared by C4LSP (editor),\n  C4Script.dll (ORCv2 scripts) and C4Api.dll (C API v1-v3 for tools). C4.exe, C4LSP and scripts run the same lowering\n  driver, so editor errors equal build errors by construction.\n\n## 2. The pipeline now\n\n| # | Phase | Owner | In -> out | Threads |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Register sources | `SourceManager` | CLI / projects.toml / Bedrock umbrella -> sources (text never rewritten) | N |\n| 2 | MacroPass | `Macro/` (R8) | file tokens -> a `MacroLayout` per file + exported table | per file |\n| 3 | InteropPass | `Interop/` + CBind + clang (R8) | extern directives -> binding units, foreign objects, libs | per file |\n| 4 | Parse | `CompilerInstance`, `Lexer/`, `Parser/` (R7) | file + layout -> AST (recovering per declaration) + include closures | N |\n| 5 | Program model | `Model/Builder` (R9, R4) | declarations -> `ProgramModel`, resolved on demand, one visibility rule | 1 |\n| 6 | Lowering | `Backend/Lowering` (R2, R10) -> `Backend/HIR` -> `Backend/MIR` (R5) | records -> HIR -> MIR; checks on the CFG | -j, one pass |\n| 7 | LLVM emission | `Backend/CodeGen` (R3, emit-only), `Target/` (R11) | LoweredProgram -> partition modules, stack maps (R16) | per partition |\n| 8 | Optimize + assemble | `ProgramOutput`, `PartitionMerge` (R12), `ObjectCache` | partitions -> objects (Dist: merged, optimized whole, split) | -j |\n| 9 | Runtime + link | `RuntimeObjects`, the TargetAbi's link | objects + C4Runtime + foreign objects -> executable | 1 |\n\n## 3. What each review point became\n\n| # | Outcome | Commits |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | Incremental builds: up to 256 partitions; a build server, Nuke's default for Debug and Development, that serves function-body, inline, template-body and global-value edits byte-identically to a one-shot build (a header constant on the IED server 2.9 -> 1.8 s at -O3, Claymore's editor 4.6 -> 2.3 s); signatures, types, includes and macros rebuild cold inside the server | 53eeff3c, 7a690418, 9028199e, bde92795, f6b4f6af, 823e557c |\n| R2 | One lowering driver; the old copied loop never lowered template-made bodies (BUG-482) | 24892b9b |\n| R3 | CodeGenDriver split; codegen emits only | 24892b9b |\n| R4 | One visibility rule (D-88) | 67db64d8 |\n| R5 | MIR, a control-flow graph between HIR and LLVM | a3230ae2 |\n| R6 | `[compile_time]` functions (D-91), their MIR interpreted | 814e52b8 |\n| R7 | Error-tolerant parser | cabed2f3 |\n| R8 | Macros over tokens with locations; bindings as units | 75ce8e8e |\n| R9 | Declarations resolve on demand, no round caps | 65633bc1 |\n| R10 | Lowering's model changes as requests; one pass on threads; TSan gate | cf2faf93 |\n| R11 | One TargetAbi per build | d9e31bf1 |\n| R12 | One emission path (D-90) | 5af1a6f3 |\n| R13 | Reflection scope (D-89) | 84b10f8c |\n| R14 | Namespace `C4Compiler`; docs current | ec1cea28 |\n| R15 | C4Api v2 and v3: a program's model through the C API | 330e8a06, 0aad2eee, 4199b58d |\n| R16 | Precise GC: heap objects, roots, typed buffers, reflected values, and stack maps on by default (run time at parity; exe +4-10%; one-thread -O0 compile +5-9%) | e11a1d3b, 7cb4582c, c416112f, 2f462091, 55d9968d, 03e2c2b4, d8e279be, 26e5f261, f17a7a63 |\n\nOwner's decisions: one visibility rule (R4); `[compile_time]` (R6); precise heap and stack maps now (R16); GC trigger\n115% (549d1f23); a script host keeps its `Script` reachable; README.md deleted.\n\nBugs fixed on the way: BUG-421, 435, 441, 476, 478-508, 510 - among them BUG-497 (Linux heap corruption: a socket's\nsends and receives shared one error text, 0e0d7d81), BUG-503 (job systems all pinned core 0, 92be3a22), BUG-508 (the\nobject cache's compiler identity and trust, 3ffdc447).\n\n## 4. Verification (chat AB, HEAD 823e557c)\n\n`nuke gates` all steps; Linux suites; `nuke test ied-server` 571/571; `nuke conformance` 64 + schema 453/0 + server\nchecks 559 (2 skipped); Nuke 362; frontend 508; ai-evals selftest; Claymore 84/84 with its editor and client;\nAmmoCrate 54/54 (Windows and Linux); JRPGToolkit; LS 81/82 (its two house tests follow the LS session's work in progress).\n\n## 5. Open\n\n- BUG-509: compiler crashes that do not reproduce; the evidence points at this machine's hardware (five 0x1A\n  MEMORY_MANAGEMENT bugchecks, a fatal WHEA NMI, bad memory regions removed, illegal instructions on valid code). Test the\n  RAM and CPU: MemTest86 (4 passes, both DIMMs, then each alone), the latest BIOS with defaults (PBO, Curve Optimizer and\n  EXPO off), HWiNFO64 during a long build, a per-core stress test (OCCT or Core Cycler).\n- A reboot clears three test processes stuck in termination (and `%TEMP%\\ab-stuck`).\n- JRPGToolkit is not pushed (its Gitea repository is empty and on another branch) - the owner's call.\n\n## Diagram\n\n{{board:mermaid:Layer 1}}\n","by":"ai"}
]
}
